.TH SPP-DEPLOY-PUSH 1 "November 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
deploy-push \- Push local project modifications and migrations to a remote SPP target server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php deploy:push
[\fItarget\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain=\fIdomain\fR]
[\fB\-\-domains=\fId1,d2\fR]
[\fB\-\-app=\fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-apps=\fIa1,a2\fR]
[\fB\-\-global\-apps\fR]
[\fB\-\-framework\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-framework\fR]
[\fB\-\-key=\fItoken\fR]
[\fB\-\-artifact=\fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-no-db\fR]
[\fB\-\-no-files\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deploy:push
synchronizes the local project state with a remote SPP deployment target using differential
state comparison. The command executes live 6-stage telemetry progress indicators reporting target
health, workspace scanning, differential calculations, payload packaging, transmission, and
remote server hook execution. It natively supports multi-directory topology routing, allowing
framework files, domain applications, and global applications to be synchronized simultaneously
across heterogeneous destination webroots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I target
The name of the target server configured in \fB.sppdeploy.yml\fR (e.g., \fIproduction\fR, \fIstaging\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-domain= domain
Scope deployment to a specific domain directory (e.g. \fIdomains/example.com\fR) and its live webroot.
.TP
.BI \-\-domains= d1,d2
Comma-separated list of domains to deploy.
.TP
.BI \-\-app= name
Scope deployment to a specific application (resolves both global apps in \fIsrc/\fR and domain apps in \fIdomains/<domain>/src/\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-apps= a1,a2
Comma-separated list of applications to deploy.
.TP
.BR \-\-global\-apps
Scope deployment to all global applications residing in \fIsrc/\fR and \fIapps/\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-framework\-only
Deploy strictly the framework core (\fIspp/\fR, \fIpublic/\fR, root entrypoints) to the framework directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-framework
Exclude framework core files when deploying scoped applications or domains.
.TP
.BI \-\-key= token
Authentication secret token override for authenticating with the target deployment receiver.
.TP
.BI \-\-artifact= path
Specify custom location for the compiled differential archive artifact.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry-run
Perform differential calculation and display files to create, update, and delete without transferring changes.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-db
Skip database schema scanning, comparison, and migration.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-files
Skip filesystem file scanning and synchronization, executing only schema updates and post-deploy hooks.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude-files= p1,p2
Exclude specific files or glob patterns from deployment push (e.g., \fI*.local.yml\fR, \fIdata/*.sqlite\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude-data
Exclude all SQLite database files and database schema synchronizations from live push.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude-tables= t1,t2
Exclude specific database tables from remote schema synchronization (e.g., \fItest_*\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-silent
Suppress verbose deployment output and display only a concise one-line status summary.
.TP
.BR \-\-quiet ", " \-q
Quiet mode: suppress all output except critical errors.
.TP
.BR \-\-force
Proceed with deployment even when pre-flight checks report non-fatal warnings or version drift.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.IP 1. 4
Validates connectivity, PHP runtime versions, database status, and ext-zip availability on the remote target.
.IP 2. 4
Acquires a distributed deployment lock on the target server to prevent concurrent deploy collisions.
.IP 3. 4
Scans the local workspace using \fBProjectScanner\fR and \fBDbScanner\fR to compute SHA-256 state vectors.
.IP 4. 4
Dispatches local state signatures to the remote receiver to calculate differential deltas.
.IP 5. 4
Assembles differential updates into an encrypted deployment archive via \fBZipArchive\fR.
.IP 6. 4
Streams the archive to the remote deployment receiver, where updates are extracted, backups are created, and migrations execute.
.IP 7. 4
Releases the distributed deployment lock and logs comprehensive audit records.
.SH SEE ALSO
